# Local AI Chat App

A clean, interactive chatbot application built with **Streamlit** that runs entirely on your local machine using **Ollama**. Your prompts and conversation history stay 100% private.

## ⚙️ How It Works
* **Frontend:** Streamlit handles the user interface, chat bubbles, and input states.
* **Backend:** The app sends user inputs via an API request to your local Ollama service.
* **Inference:** Ollama runs the LLM locally on your CPU/GPU and streams responses back to the chat UI.

## 🛠️ Setup & Installation

### 1. Download & Start Ollama
1. Download Ollama for your operating system from [ollama.com](https://ollama.com).
2. Open your terminal and download your preferred model (e.g., Qwen2.5 Coder):
   ```bash
   ollama run qwen2.5-coder:14b
   ```
3. Keep Ollama running in the background.

### 2. Clone the Repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com
cd your-repo-name
```

### 3. Set Up Your Virtual Environment (venv)
Initialize your local environment and install the required dependencies:

```bash
# Create the virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Activate it (Mac/Linux)
source venv/bin/activate

# Activate it (Windows PowerShell)
# .\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

# Install requirements
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## 🚀 Running the App
Once your environment is active and Ollama is running, launch the chat interface:

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```
Your browser will automatically open to `http://localhost:8501` with your local chat interface ready to go!

